<title>USA: Citicorp consolidates entire ad account -WSJ.</title>
<headline>Citicorp consolidates entire ad account -WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citicorp withdrew its entire $500 million global advertising account from three agencies and handed it over to Young &amp; Rubicam, the Wall Street Journal reported.</p>
<p>The move was a stunning blow to the three firms: WPP Group's J. Walter Thompson, True North Communications' Foote, Cone &amp; Belding and the Interpublic Group's Lowe Group, the paper said in its electronic edition.</p>
<p>Citicorp made the move as part of an effort to greatly expand its worldwide name recognition, the paper said.</p>
</text>
